  "title": "Kourovka problem 9.42 (main)",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "pdf-text-entry",
    "text": "Let Ω be a countable set and let D be the set of total order relations on Ω for\nwhich Ω is order-isomorphic with Q. Does there exist a transitive proper subgroup G\nof Sym(Ω) which is transitive on D?                                  P. M. Neumann\n  ∗ An affirmative answer is consistent with the ZFC axioms of set theory\n(S. M. Corson, S. Shelah, Preprint, 2025, https://arxiv.org/abs/2503.12997).",
